Design a premium banking and fintech interface inspired by modern products such as Stripe, Mercury, Revolut, Vercel and Microsoft 365.

Technology
• Tailwind CSS
• shadcn/ui
• Lucide Icons
• Responsive design using modern CSS Grid/Flexbox

Design Principles
• Professional banking aesthetic
• Minimal and clean layouts
• Consistent spacing (8px grid system)
• Rounded corners (12–16px)
• Soft shadows
• High visual hierarchy
• Plenty of whitespace
• Consistent typography
• No emojis
• No unnecessary gradients
• No glassmorphism unless specifically requested
• Smooth, subtle animations only (Framer Motion where appropriate)

Accessibility (Highest Priority)
The primary audience includes users aged 50–70.

Always prioritize:
• Large readable typography (minimum 16px body text)
• High colour contrast
• Large touch targets (minimum 44px)
• Simple navigation
• Clear labels
• Avoid hidden interactions
• Keyboard accessibility
• Screen reader compatibility
• WCAG AA compliance where possible

Mobile First
Every page must function correctly on:
• Desktop
• Tablet
• Mobile

Authentication, transaction approval, call detection, and OTP flows should be designed mobile-first.

Internationalization
Design all layouts to support:
• English
• Hindi
• Punjabi

Do not hardcode English-only layouts. Components should accommodate varying text lengths.

Banking Experience
The interface should feel trustworthy rather than flashy.

Prioritize:
• Security
• Clarity
• Confidence
• Explainability

Users should immediately understand:
• Why a transaction was blocked
• Why additional authentication is required
• What action they should take next

Consistency
Reuse existing components whenever possible.

Prefer extending existing UI over creating duplicate components.

Maintain consistent spacing, colours, typography, icons, and interaction patterns across the entire application.
